  "body_html": "<h1>Convex Games Have Nonempty Core</h1>\n<p><strong>Theorem.</strong> If a finite TU game is convex, then its core is nonempty.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>Sketch</p>\n<p>Convexity implies the balancedness inequalities required by\nBondareva-Shapley. Applying\n[[game_theory.cooperative_game.bondareva_shapley]] then gives\nnonemptiness of the core.</p>\n<h2>Lean Status</h2>\n<p>The Lean module defines the relevant core and convex-game predicates. This\ntheorem remains a blueprint target depending on the Bondareva-Shapley route.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.17, Thm 17.55] Maschler, Solan, Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>.</li>\n</ul>",
